  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Armies of the Lord**: rare: 14 archived performances [2]\n- **Cold at Night**: rare: 8 archived performances [2]\n- **Rotten Stinking Mouthpiece**: back after 142 archived shows (1579 days); rare: 8 archived performances [2]\n- **Dawn of Revelation**: rare: 12 archived performances [2]\n- **Song for Black Sabbath's Second North American Tour**: back after 179 archived shows (2431 days); rare: 6 archived performances [2]\n- **Rescue Breathing**: back after 142 archived shows (1579 days); rare: 3 archived performances [2]\n- **For the Krishnacore Bands**: back after 62 archived shows (800 days); rare: 8 archived performances [2]\n- **Great Pirates**: rare: 13 archived performances [2]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tMG2025-12-14** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 21 songs; 107 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: No Children [1]\n- Cameron Ralston played a song he had not heard before, succeeding despite minimal preparation time [1]\n- The band expressed gratitude to the crew and Brandon Eggleston as the tour concluded [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tMG2025-12-14**: taped by Kyle Kennelly & Emerald Green; transferred by Kyle Kennelly; source: SBD > PCM-A10 + FR-AV2 > DPA 4060s (Healy on stage) + FR-AV2 > Neumann KM-184s PAS FOB [1]. Also: Recording the show required a steep venue fee, which was covered by collective financial contributions from fans [1]",
